    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (`AcceptanceBase` is the abstract harness).\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` computed and stored at creation.\n\n**Level formula** (in the new `AssignMembershipLevel` step): start at 1, +1 if an email is present, +1 if `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3 (level 4 left free for tenure).\n\nChanges:\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `membershipLevel` field (`membership_level` column) with getter/setter.\n- **`AssignMembershipLevel.java`** (new) \u2014 computes the level from the owner's already-settled email and namesake count.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step in after `assignNamesakeCount`, under the same transaction governance.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 removed the `membershipTier` derivation; `membershipLevel` now maps straight through by name.\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel=` (verified in the run: `AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-LEV-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-04 membershipLevel=3`).\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` string property with a `membershipLevel` int32 (min 1, max 4), driving the generated `OwnerDto`.\n- **`AssignHouseholdSize.java`** \u2014 dropped the now-stale GOLD-tier reference from its javadoc.\n- **DB schemas** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `membership_level` column.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` (expects `$.membershipLevel == 3` for an owner with email and no namesakes) passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS` for the whole suite.\n\nNote: `householdSize` is still assigned/stored but no longer influences membership (it previously drove the removed GOLD tier and isn't part of the response schema); I left that data-collection step intact as out of scope.",
